  "summary": "Spring Chickens and More to Hatch\nThe spate of newbuilding activity across different tanker sectors could be evidence that a lemming-like approach to supply analysis is well underway. Besides the obvious consequence of oversupply, short-term market players seem to propagate the myth that vessels older than 15 years will be forced into an early grave. It is important to remember that the intended useful life of a tanker is 25 years and explicit age restriction policies have never been widely adopted by the oil companies.",
